{#
contacts/_page_shell.html.twig — a contacts page at full size: the mailbox,
with the mail column put away and the address book's dock given the row.

Chosen by contacts/_layout.html.twig for anything that is not a navigation
inside the pane. `data-contacts-full` on the shell is the whole difference from
a mailbox with the pane open (see app.css), so leaving it is one attribute and
not a visit: contacts--pane#reveal takes it off when a message is opened from
the contact, and the mail column slides in beside a contact that never left
the page — same DOM, same scroll position.

The mail side is the thread page's: no list behind it, said to be empty, so a
list is fetched the first time one is wanted rather than rendered for a column
nobody sees. Below lg, where the mail cannot sit beside the pane, a message
opened here is still an ordinary visit (see mail--open-in-pane).
#}
{% extends '_layout/_mailbox.html.twig' %}

{% set contactsFull = true %}

{% block message_list %}{% endblock %}
{% block inbox_tabs %}{% endblock %}
{% block list_rendered %}0{% endblock %}

{# The page's own content, in the frame the dock would have fetched it into —
   _pane_layout's, plus `advance`: while the pane has the row, a navigation
   inside it is a navigation of the page, and the address says so. Taken off
   with the full state, when the mail's address becomes the page's again. The
   flashes go to the toast region the full layout already has. #}
{% block contacts_dock %}
    {% set contactsPaneBody %}
        <turbo-frame id="contacts-pane-frame" data-turbo-action="advance" class="flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1">
            <div data-contacts-page class="@container relative flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0 min-w-0 overflow-hidden">
                {{ block('contacts_content') }}
            </div>
        </turbo-frame>
    {% endset %}
    {% include '_partials/_contacts_pane.html.twig' with { contactsPaneBody: contactsPaneBody } %}
{% endblock %}
